  "generality_evidence": {
    "adm_3_inertness": "ADM-3 returns PASS on all fifteen items. That is the expected result rather than a suppressed one: no R4 failure is attributed to exclusion by explicit stem negation as its earliest causal layer, and no competitor in the cohort is defeated solely by an absent finding that grounds nothing else. The rule is shown to fire on a constructed input in the unit tests and again as a positive control in the G1 wave.",
    "authorship_disclosure": "The role-blind option labels and the demanded response classes were authored in the same session that ran this replay, by a party that had read the R4 independent verdicts. That is the residual risk of this gate and it is stated rather than hidden. Three structural constraints bound it: every label is a choice among a closed enumeration rather than free text, no artifact can express which option is a key or which item an option belongs to, and the rules that consume the labels contain no item identity and no clinical content. The rules are additionally exercised against synthetic inputs in the unit tests, where they separate cases the R4 cohort does not contain.",
    "demanded_class_artifact_carries_no_option_text": "ASSERTED_BY_TEST",
    "label_pool_is_role_blind": "The pool is flat, keyed by normalized option text, and carries no role, key marker, item id or option position. Identical option text resolves to one label everywhere.",
    "no_item_id_or_replayed_option_text_in_production_code": "ASSERTED_BY_TEST: tests/test_qgen_profiles_and_g0.py::test_no_production_module_names_a_replayed_item_or_its_clinical_content"
  },
